{"id": "EUVD-2026-108871", "enisaUuid": "828abd1b-08da-3596-964b-3a22b15c183d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: video-i2c: use vb2_video_unregister_device on driver removal\n\nThe driver uses vb2_fop_release() as its file release operation, so\nvb2_video_unregister_device() should be used instead of\nvideo_unregister_device() during driver removal.\n\nThis ensures that the vb2 queue is properly disconnected before the\nvideo device is unregistered.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97adc8cd04df2085f7fd437838005f3bb16bafae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7afb0c24a761c2367e5fa87a9941d67d373c127", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8fba9f66019d4c83235c4219ff8edeb7e3af20d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82e432c9ebfa13fb8d47d6d550be5d7d2a84a8ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56384b486b80ce4a2bc93689aae49995f908f90d", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98915"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98915", "GHSA-fcx8-m762-264h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0243e48e-a666-345f-9244-8ef29ec41a67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <97adc8cd04df2085f7fd437838005f3bb16bafae"}, {"id": "1725cfdd-4640-3b6e-a4aa-7f72f0c394e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <b8fba9f66019d4c83235c4219ff8edeb7e3af20d"}, {"id": "1ddc9a5e-8730-3628-bea8-cba74e8bec10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.12.111"}, {"id": "3889376c-2eed-3697-b2a0-8d6d855e9978", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <b7afb0c24a761c2367e5fa87a9941d67d373c127"}, {"id": "7d086e8f-cf2d-3971-9cc6-0b26b338f62a", "product"